G5465.definition:
χαλάω, -ῶ
[in LXX: (Jer.38:6) (שָׁלַח pi.), etc. ;]
(a) to slacken, loosen;
(b) to let loose, let go;
(with) to lower, let down: with accusative of thing(s), Mrk.2:4, Luk.5:4-5, Act.9:25 27:17, 30; with accusative of person(s) (cf. Je, l.with), pass., 2Co.11:33.†

G5467.definition:
χαλεπός, -ή, -όν
[in LXX: Isa.18:2 (יָרֵא), Wis.3:19, Sir.3:21, al. ;]
hard;
(a) hard to do or deal with, difficult;
(b) hard to bear, painful, grievous: καιροί, 2Ti.3:1;
(with) of persons, hard to deal with, harsh, fierce, savage: Mat.8:28.†
